COLUMNS
int ID
int LightParamID // the LightParams row (copy IDs included) whose day this key belongs to: every value is one (proven from the bytes); it is also in the section's relationship map, with the same value on every row
int Time // the key's time of day in half-minutes, 0 to 2870 (< 2880): proven from the bytes; in layout 360DA016 its pallet words carry bit 16 (0x10000), which is not part of the value -- read it as 16 bits
int Field_02 // not established (colour)
int Field_03 // not established (colour)
int Field_04 // not established (colour)
int Field_05 // not established (colour)
int SkyBand1Color // a colour, 0xRRGGBB in the low 24 bits, stored as OceanCloseColor (mask with 0xFFFFFF): the colour the viewer gives a water reflection that finds no scene (no sky is drawn before Stage 12). That it is the sky's first band is the public definitions' name, not proven; it was chosen by measurement among the six sky columns they name (fields 4-9): at 12:00 Durotar's LightParams 5985 holds (246,178,88), the nearest of the six to the sky just above the far hills in two noon captures of the game, (249,193,116) and (215,147,81) -- 31.9 and 44.4 away, the next nearest 67.9 and 52.9
