int OceanCloseColor // a colour, 0xRRGGBB in the low 24 bits (signed 25-bit storage: a few rows read back with the upper byte 0xFF, so mask with 0xFFFFFF): the colour and its byte order are proven from the bytes; that it is the near ocean colour is the public definitions' name, not proven
int OceanFarColor // as OceanCloseColor: the far ocean colour (name not proven)
int RiverCloseColor // as OceanCloseColor: the near river/lake colour (name supported by the Durotar reference fit, Southfury River)
int RiverFarColor // as OceanCloseColor: the far river/lake colour (name supported by the Durotar reference fit)
