COMMENT Written for WoW Model Viewer's light catalogue (wow::LightCatalog: the zone light's water colours,
COMMENT docs/world-viewer/09-liquids.md). The layouts come from public table definitions, read as hypotheses: every column
COMMENT the catalogue reads (database.xml, table LightData) was checked against the clients' own bytes. A neutral name that
COMMENT two layouts share is the same column: Retail 12.1.5 (6ABF2921) and PTR 12.1.7 (360DA016) agree on every column 0-19
COMMENT of all 19881 rows they share, read at one field later in 360DA016; Classic Era and MoP Classic (70C6CD80) keep
COMMENT fields 0-19 in Retail's order (each water colour equals Retail's same column on 562 to 595 of 638 Classic Era keys
COMMENT and 3334 to 3356 of 3371 MoP Classic keys that Retail shares with four distinct water colours, another column on
COMMENT at most 10; SkyBand1Color equals Retail's on 1222 of 1321 Classic Era keys, 4350 of 4491 MoP Classic keys and
COMMENT 1228 of 1327 Classic Beta keys that Retail shares where Retail's value differs from its other colour columns,
COMMENT another column on at most 3). Every field is listed in file order, so the positions are right for the layouts
COMMENT below. Classic Beta's water colours are 0 on most of its rows, among them every map default and zone light of
COMMENT Eastern Kingdoms and Kalimdor: a key whose four water colours are all 0 carries no water colour. A layout not
COMMENT listed here is not read.

